---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Kirian Luna"
  description="Privacy policy and data protection principles for kirian.dev. Details on data handling, analytics, and contact information."
  lang="en"
>
  <Navbar />

  <main id="main-content" class="min-h-screen bg-grayscale-1">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-0 pt-28 pb-16 flex flex-col gap-10">
      <!-- Header -->
      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h1 class="font-figgle text-3xl text-grayscale-12 tracking-tight select-none">
          privacy policy.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-grayscale-11 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Last updated: October 23, 2026. This policy explains how information is handled when you visit kirian.dev or interact with its services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Overview -->
      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-grayscale-11 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="font-figgle text-2xl text-grayscale-12 tracking-tight select-none">
          1. entity identity & scope.
        </h2>
        <p>
          This website (<strong>https://kirian.dev</strong>) is operated by Kirian Luna, an independent software engineer based in Limón, Costa Rica. Your privacy is respected and prioritized through minimal data collection, zero third-party advertising trackers, and transparent engineering practices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Information Collected -->
      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-grayscale-11 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="font-figgle text-2xl text-grayscale-12 tracking-tight select-none">
          2. information collected & purpose.
        </h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-grayscale-12 text-sm font-semibold">Direct Communication Data</h3>
            <p class="mt-1">
              When you submit the contact form or send an email, we receive the name, email address, and message content you provide. This data is exclusively used to reply to your inquiry, discuss business opportunities, or provide requested technical information. It is never sold, leased, or distributed to marketing third parties.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-grayscale-12 text-sm font-semibold">Analytics & Performance Metrics</h3>
            <p class="mt-1">
              We employ a privacy-first instance of PostHog to aggregate anonymous aggregate pageviews, referral sources, and high-level engagement. PostHog is configured without cross-site tracking cookies and does not build invasive personal profiles.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-grayscale-12 text-sm font-semibold">Reaction & Engagement Storage</h3>
            <p class="mt-1">
              Article reactions are tallied via secure serverless Redis instances (Upstash). A pseudonymous, non-reversible cryptographic hash of your client IP and User-Agent is stored transiently for rate-limiting and deduplication only; no raw personal identity is linked to blog reactions.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Third-Party Infrastructure -->
      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-grayscale-11 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="font-figgle text-2xl text-grayscale-12 tracking-tight select-none">
          3. third-party infrastructure.
        </h2>
        <p>
          This site relies on reputable, industry-standard infrastructure providers:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-xs text-grayscale-11">
          <li><strong>Vercel</strong>: Edge hosting, content delivery network (CDN), and DNS routing.</li>
          <li><strong>Formspree</strong>: Form submission processing and secure email dispatch.</li>
          <li><strong>Upstash</strong>: Serverless Redis datastore for anonymous reaction counts.</li>
          <li><strong>PostHog</strong>: First-party telemetry and aggregated analytics.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: User Rights -->
      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-grayscale-11 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="font-figgle text-2xl text-grayscale-12 tracking-tight select-none">
          4. your rights & data inquiries.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Regardless of your jurisdiction (including GDPR, CCPA, and Costa Rica Law No. 8968 on the Protection of Personal Data), you retain the right to request access to, correction of, or permanent deletion of any personal data you have transmitted via the contact form.
        </p>
        <p>
          To exercise your rights or ask questions regarding this policy, contact Kirian Luna directly at:
        </p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-grayscale-12">
          Email: <a href="mailto:kirianluna.u@gmail.com" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-9">kirianluna.u@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <Footer />
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
